.TH TERMIPDF 1 "August 2026" "termipdf 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termipdf \- a modern PDF editor with an embedded terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termipdf
[\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBTermiPDF\fR is a PyQt6 desktop PDF editor with a built-in terminal for
batch operations.  It opens any PDF, lets you annotate, edit pages, and
exposes every feature as a typed command.
.PP
If \fIPATH\fR is given, that PDF is opened on launch.  Otherwise
\fBtermipdf\fR starts with an empty workspace.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
\fBViewer\fR
Single-page or continuous-scroll, zoom, fit-to-window, outline (TOC)
sidebar, thumbnail rail.
.TP
\fBAnnotate\fR
Freehand ink, multi-colour highlights, sticky notes, shapes
(rect, ellipse, arrow), and Unicode text insertion (including Bangla).
.TP
\fBEdit pages\fR
Delete, rotate, swap, split, merge, reorder, extract, and generate
new PDFs from current pages.
.TP
\fBTools\fR
QR-share popups, image-to-PDF conversion, full-text search with
auto-highlight, undo/redo, save.
.TP
\fBThemes\fR
Dark (Dracula/Nord) and light (Edge-like); auto-detected from your OS
preference and persisted across sessions.
.TP
\fBTerminal\fR
An embedded terminal docks at the bottom of the window.  Every
feature is available as a typed command.  Press \fBCtrl+T\fR (or
\fBCtrl+\`\fR) to show it, then type \fBhelp\fR to list every command.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a PDF.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save annotations into the current PDF.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Toggle the embedded terminal.
.TP
.B Ctrl+`
Toggle the embedded terminal (alternate).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T
Toggle between dark and light themes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Find text on the page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Print the current document.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/TermiPDF/TermiPDF.conf
Persistent settings (theme, recent files, dock layout).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/TermiPDF/
Crash logs and autosave data.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README at \fIhttps://github.com/shuv-on/TermiPDF\fR for
the full command reference and example workflows.
